# LibreWolf search-config.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M4-06 ("Ship the LibreWolf search configuration on Android")
#
# Upstream files touched
# -----------------------
#   third_party/application-services/components/remote_settings/src/client.rs
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/secret_settings_preferences.xml
#
# Line numbers are from the ESR tree (firefox-153.0esr, ./version.android), AFTER
# the patches listed before this one in assets/patches/android.txt.
#
#
# Where Android's search configuration really comes from
# -------------------------------------------------------
# Desktop LibreWolf replaces services/settings/dumps/main/search-config-v2.json
# (scripts/librewolf-patches.py) and Gecko's SearchService reads it. Fenix never
# reads that file. Its engine list is built by android-components'
# SearchMiddleware (feature/search/.../middleware/SearchMiddleware.kt:61-94):
# with Settings.useRemoteSearchConfiguration true it uses
# SearchEngineSelectorRepository, which calls the app-services `search`
# component (Rust, third_party/application-services/components/search) through
# the app-services RemoteSettingsService; that client serves the
# `search-config-v2` and `search-config-icons` collections from the dumps
# compiled INTO libmegazord.so by remote_settings/src/client.rs:95-103
# (packaged_collections!, include_str! of dumps/main/<collection>.json) -- and,
# since rs-blocker-android.patch (LW-M4-08) made sync() a no-op and
# make_request() an error, from nowhere else. So the packaged dump IS the
# configuration, for the life of the build.
#
# That is the same file format as desktop's dump (one Remote Settings
# collection, {"data": [...], "timestamp": N}), so scripts/librewolf-patches.py
# now copies assets/search-config-v2.json over
# third_party/application-services/components/remote_settings/dumps/main/
# search-config-v2.json for android targets too, rewrites the .timestamp
# sidecar client.rs reads at :95-103, and does the same for the icons
# collection -- see android_search_config() in that script, which asserts every
# path it writes (landmine L4) and drops icon records android-components cannot
# decode (SearchEngineReader.kt:390-399 decodes svg, x-icon, png and jpeg; the
# DuckDuckGo *pdf* record would otherwise be the FIRST match for "ddg" in
# findMatchingIcon (SearchEngineSelectorRepository.kt:152-170) and the default
# engine would ship with the generic icon).
#
#
# What this patch does
# ---------------------
# 1. client.rs -- packages the Mojeek icon. Attachments are only served from the
#    binary if their record id is in the packaged_attachments! list
#    (client.rs:115-, one include_bytes! per entry, looked up by record id at
#    :516 load_packaged_attachment(&record.id)). Mojeek is the one engine
#    LibreWolf adds that upstream has no icon for, so its id
#    2c4b8834-030c-4097-a887-c7506689095c is added; the file and its
#    <id>.meta.json ({location, hash, size} -- app-services' sidecar shape, NOT
#    desktop's full-record .meta.json) are written by the patcher from
#    assets/2c4b8834-030c-4097-a887-c7506689095c, with the hash and size
#    computed from the file. (The hash inside assets/*.meta.json and inside the
#    shared icons record is a9c0b3d3..., which is NOT the sha256 of the file
#    LibreWolf ships (793d49ae...); the patcher fixes the Android copies of both
#    so validation cannot fail on a stale digest.)
#    Startpage's record id acae3d3c-b09e-47f0-a9e5-57980d21fc4a is added too:
#    upstream ships the file and its sidecar in dumps/main/attachments/ but
#    never lists the id, so the record is served and its attachment is not --
#    the engine appears with the generic icon. The remaining three LibreWolf
#    icon records (ddg svg, wikipedia png and ico) are packaged upstream. The
#    patcher asserts that every kept record id is in this list (client.rs or
#    this patch) and that each sidecar's hash/size agree with the record,
#    because a file that is present but unlisted is exactly the failure that
#    cannot be seen from a build that compiles.
#
# 2. Settings.kt -- useRemoteSearchConfiguration becomes a constant `true`. It
#    was a preference defaulting to the FML flag remote-search-configuration
#    (nimbus.fml.yaml:899-906, default true). With no-nimbus.patch the FML
#    default is the only source, but an upstream flip of that default on a
#    rebase would silently route Fenix to the OTHER path --
#    BundledSearchEnginesStorage over assets/search/list.json and
#    assets/searchplugins/*.xml, Google default, partner codes -- with every
#    gate still green on the sources. A constant cannot flip. Same rationale as
#    fission-isolation.patch and isolated-process.patch.
#
# 3. SecretSettingsFragment.kt / secret_settings_preferences.xml -- the hidden
#    debug switch for that preference is removed. It wrote the SharedPreference
#    directly (SharedPreferenceUpdater) and its toggle also (un)registered the
#    Remote Settings sync worker; with a constant behind it the row could only
#    ever be a dead toggle.
#
# The engine set itself is not in this diff: it is data (assets/
# search-config-v2.json, 92 records: DuckDuckGo No-AI as the global default,
# Startpage, Mojeek, Wikipedia in 88 locales) and it stays a plain copy, exactly
# like desktop, so that a rebase never rejects on a 150-record JSON hunk.
#
#
# What this patch does NOT cover, with owners
# --------------------------------------------
#   * The legacy bundled list (assets/search/list.json + searchplugins/*.xml)
#     still ships in the APK. It is unreachable (item 2), and a static scan of
#     it does not describe what the user sees -- which is why
#     scripts/android-smoke.sh --check-search reads the engine list from the
#     RUNNING app (Settings > Search > Default search engine) and runs a real
#     query, not the XML.
#   * Search suggestions and trending searches: no-suggest.patch (LW-M4-11).
#     LibreWolf's engine records carry suggestion URLs; they are only used when
#     the user turns suggestions on.
#   * search-telemetry-v2 (the third search dump) feeds Glean: no-glean.patch.
#
#
# Ordering
# ---------
# Shares Settings.kt with no-adjust, no-onboarding, no-gms and no-suggest, and
# client.rs with rs-blocker-android. Measured per file the way no-suggest's
# were (replay from the pristine ESR copy, list order and once per partner with
# this patch moved in front of it): see scripts/check-patch-order.py's
# REVIEWED_ORDER_FREE rows for this patch. Listed last in
# assets/patches/android.txt.
#
#
# Verification
# -------------
#   ./scripts/android-smoke.sh --check-search --serial <dev> --apk <apk>
# opens Settings > Search > Default search engine on the running build and
# reads the engine names off the screen (Mojeek present, DuckDuckGo No-AI
# selected), then types a query into the toolbar and inspects the URL it lands
# on for partner/attribution parameters. Evidence: docs/android/evidence/lw-m4-06/.
